{
 "method": "tau_q_s: shift (s) by which ur_joint_states rows are stamped LATE relative to the fresh `command` table, i.e. the row stamped t_rel_s holds the arm state measured at t_rel_s - tau. Found by minimising mean_j mean_t |q_j(t) - cmd_j(t - tau)| over a 5 ms grid of tau in [0, 1.5] s, both streams linearly interpolated onto a uniform 100 Hz grid spanning the overlap minus the first 1.6 s and last 0.2 s; resid_rad is that minimum (resid_rad_at_zero is the same metric at tau = 0). tau_q_xcorr_s: independent second method -- the tau maximising the summed per-joint Pearson correlation between d/dt q(t) and d/dt cmd(t - tau) on the same grid (offset-immune); xcorr_r is that sum divided by 6. tau_tcp_s: how much LATER ur_joint_states is stamped than tcp_pose, from min_s mean|p_tcp(t) - p_fk(t + s)| with p_fk = UR7e nominal-DH forward kinematics (ur_gello_bringup.ur_kin.fk) of q plus a 0.174 m tool-z offset; positive means tcp_pose is FRESHER. tcp_resid_mm is that minimum in mm. Cause: gello_recorder GUI stamps rows at callback execution time and the single rclpy spin thread is starved by depth recording, so each table is stale by QoS depth / publish rate. Only ur_joint_states is corrected in the LeRobot release.",
 "grid_s": 0.005,
 "skip_head_s": 1.6,
 "skip_tail_s": 0.2,
